Stop extract_dtb on a node that does not fit (D59).

parse_dtb_node returns an error when the token of a node, or the structure
of a property, does not fit in the data. extract_dtb then reads the same
entry again, with no end. The walker rejects the blob there, and this patch
makes binwalk-ng reject it too. test/corpus/testdata/walk/dtb-6.bin and
dtb-7.bin hold such blobs.

--- a/src/formats/dtb.rs
+++ b/src/formats/dtb.rs
@@ -360,6 +360,11 @@
                     // Update offsets to parse the next DTB structure entry
                     previous_entry_offset = Some(entry_offset);
                     entry_offset += node.total_size;
+                } else {
+                    // The token or the property structure does not fit in
+                    // the data. Without this break, the loop reads the same
+                    // entry again with no end.
+                    break;
                 }
             }
         }
